  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nBuild a two-story planar concrete frame with bays 5 m and 7 m, both story heights 3.6 m, and all three column bases fixed. Each floor has a downward area load of 10 kN/m^2. The left beam tributary width is 4 m and the right beam width is 6 m, so apply only the converted full-span line loads: left 40 kN/m and right 60 kN/m in case D on both stories. The area load is conversion input, not an additional applied load. The completed appendix supplies C30 (E=30000 MPa, nu=0.2, G=12500 MPa, density=2500 kg/m^3), 500x500 mm columns C1 and 300x600 mm beams B1. Each physical beam has a connected, unreleased midpoint observation node and two continuous halves; each half receives its own span line-load intensity once. Run first-order linear elastic Euler-Bernoulli analysis in OpenSees with self weight off. Report ux, uz and ry at all four beam midpoints and at every column top on both stories, plus Fx/Fz/My at the three bases.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "input-data.json",
        "output-requests.json",
        "analysis-conventions.txt"
      ],
      "unresolvedFields": [],
      "expectedQuestions": []
    }
  ],
